#%PAM-1.0
# ==============================================================================
# CYBER NOIR // SWAYLOCK PAM STACK
# ==============================================================================
# Installed to /etc/pam.d/swaylock
#
# This is deliberately the stock stack. It used to carry its own
#     auth  sufficient  pam_fprintd.so timeout=10
# line, from when the lock screen was the only surface with fingerprint
# support. Fingerprint is now patched into system-auth instead -- see
# system/patch-system-auth-fprintd.sh -- which swaylock already reaches via
# login -> system-local-login -> system-login -> system-auth.
#
# Keeping both meant asking for a finger twice on the way down, so a failed
# read burned two 10s timeouts before the password prompt appeared. One entry,
# in the one stack every service includes, is the whole point.
# ==============================================================================
auth include login
